# Node Types

Three node types form the building blocks of your tunnel architecture. You only need entry and exit for a basic tunnel — relays are optional and only required when pivoting through intermediate hosts.

### Entry

Your machine. Creates a TUN interface and routes traffic into the tunnel chain.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :PORT" /%}

### Relay *(optional)*

An intermediate host that forwards traffic deeper into the network. It connects to a previous hop and listens for a subsequent hop.

{% codeblock code="wallhack relay --connect HOST:PORT --listen :PORT" /%}

### Exit

The far end of the tunnel. Unwraps packets and delivers them to the target network.

{% codeblock code="wallhack exit --connect HOST:PORT" /%}

Transport direction (`--listen` / `--connect`) is independent of node role — entry and exit nodes can either listen or connect, which is how reverse tunnels work.

